(Spark Shuffle Tuning - Field Notes \(fictional, for ingestion testing\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Symptoms of an undersized shuffle: long task tails, executor OOMs during) Tj T*
(wide joins, and spill metrics growing in the Spark UI Stages tab.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Checklist we apply before resizing the cluster:) Tj T*
(- Set spark.sql.shuffle.partitions so each shuffle partition lands) Tj T*
(  between 100 MB and 200 MB; the 200-partition default is almost) Tj T*
(  always wrong for production data volumes.) Tj T*
(- Enable Adaptive Query Execution and let it coalesce small partitions) Tj T*
(  with spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.enabled=true.) Tj T*
(- Broadcast the smaller side of a join only below ~8 GB of executor) Tj T*
(  memory per core; otherwise prefer a sort-merge join with bucketing.) Tj T*
(- Salting keys fixes skew, but try AQE skew-join handling first:) Tj T*
(  spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.enabled=true.) Tj T*
